  {
    
    "name": "Section 8",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-576270161921704522 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/429531/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_ARTICLE&editorId=576267057851532227&sectionId=576270161921704522)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggKaFIifhDY_text","label":"ggKaFIifhDY_text","default":"Precautions When Using Bakuchiol"},{"type":"html","id":"ggugp5hdMUc_text","label":"ggugp5hdMUc_text","default":"<p>Many people like bakuchiol for its gentle nature. But, it's important to follow some steps to keep your skin safe. Bakuchiol comes from the babchi plant and is found in many plant-based skincare products.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Even though it's usually safe, some fake products might cause problems. They could make your skin more sensitive to the sun or turn red. Always buy from trusted sources and check the INCI name to avoid issues.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggg60XlATN0_text","label":"ggg60XlATN0_text","default":"Patch Test Guidelines"},{"type":"html","id":"ggnChfqCboZ_text","label":"ggnChfqCboZ_text","default":"<p>Before using bakuchiol regularly, do a patch test. Apply a small amount behind your ear or on your inner forearm. Wait 24 to 48 hours to see if there's any reaction.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Start with a small amount and watch for any stinging or redness. About 10% of users might get a little irritation from pure bakuchiol.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gghPMyBMCo8_text","label":"gghPMyBMCo8_text","default":"Interaction with Other Ingredients"},{"type":"html","id":"ggtAREntZ8d_text","label":"ggtAREntZ8d_text","default":"<p>When using bakuchiol with strong exfoliants like AHAs or BHAs, use them on alternate days. This prevents over-exfoliating your skin. Use gentle cleansers and keep your skin well-hydrated for a balanced routine.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>Unrefined bakuchiol with psoralens can make your skin more sensitive to the sun. So, always protect your skin from direct UV rays. Bakuchiol is better than retinol because it causes less irritation. Adding it to your skincare routine can help your skin stay calm and healthy.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggVPgR229PS_text","label":"ggVPgR229PS_text","default":"Conclusion: Weighing Benefits Against Risks"},{"type":"html","id":"ggx5-96MkfH_text","label":"ggx5-96MkfH_text","default":"<p>This gentle retinol alternative offers promising benefits for your skin. It helps with anti-aging and brightening. Studies show it keeps cells healthy, even at high doses. It's gentle on sensitive skin and doesn't cause photosensitivity. This makes it a great choice for many.<br>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Final Thoughts on Bakuchiol Serum Usage</strong></p><p>Bakuchiol targets fine lines, acne, and uneven skin tone. It does this without causing peeling or redness, unlike retinol. It boosts collagen and keeps your skin firm and healthy.</p><p>It's important to watch for any side effects. But, they are rare. Start with a small amount and do a patch test before using it regularly.<br>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Making an Informed Decision</strong></p><p>Always do a patch test with new products. Start with a small amount and see how your skin reacts. If you have very sensitive skin, bakuchiol might be a good choice for you.</p><p>Be patient, as results take time. Think about your skin needs and goals before adding bakuchiol to your routine.</p>"}],
    "blocks": [{"type": "@app"}],
    "locales": {}
  }
